 County in the Farmland Atlas","/farmland-atlas/west-virginia/greenbrier-county"],["ARC or PLC in Greenbrier County","/arc-plc/west-virginia/greenbrier-county"],["PRF calculator","/prf"]],"story":"<p class=\"prf-lede prf-story\">As of Oct 12, the Greenbrier County record runs from 1951 to 2025, 75 years, on the middle value of the county&rsquo;s 13 grids. October to November came in under 90% of normal in 35 of those years, and it is the driest pair at 6.20 inches of normal. In 2025, August to September came in at 60% of normal on the middle of the grids. Grid 21501 had its driest year in 1963 at 70% of normal.</p>"}
